<h2 id=3D"data-flow" class=3D"max-md:pr-4" data-state=3D"closed" style=3D"c=
ursor: pointer;">Data flow</h2>
<p>An <em>integration</em> with Lattice can be unidirectional or bidirectio=
nal, supporting one or both of the following functions:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;&gt;li]:relative [&amp;&gt;li]:before:text-(color:--gray=
scale-a10) mb-3 list-none pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:pl-3 [&amp;&gt;li]:before:abso=
lute [&amp;&gt;li]:before:ml-[-22px] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:mt-[-1px] [&amp;&=
gt;li]:before:content-['=E2=A6=81'] [&amp;&gt;li]:before:self-center">
<li class=3D"">Pushing data into Lattice, such as publishing data feeds or =
integrating a new robot.</li>
<li class=3D"">Pulling data from Lattice, such as tracks generated by tower=
s to task against them.</li>
</ul>
<p>The main entry-points for these integrations are the <a data-astro-prefe=
tch=3D"viewport" class=3D"fern-mdx-link" href=3D"https://developer.anduril.=
com/reference/rest/entities/publish-entity"><code>Entities</code></a>,
<a data-astro-prefetch=3D"viewport" class=3D"fern-mdx-link" href=3D"https:/=
/developer.anduril.com/reference/rest/tasks/create-task"><code>Tasks</code>=
</a>, and <a data-astro-prefetch=3D"viewport" class=3D"fern-mdx-link" href=
=3D"https://developer.anduril.com/reference/rest/objects/list-objects"><cod=
e>Objects</code></a> APIs.
The following shows how your integration fits into the Lattice ecosystem:</=
p>
